// Answers "How do you provide your services?" on /account-type → provider
// onboarding — distinct from BusinessSize (which describes the business itself,
// not how a creator/provider operates).
enum ProviderType {
  INDIVIDUAL
  TEAM
  AGENCY
}

// Answers "How are you hiring?" on service-taker onboarding — two equal-weight
// choices, not a primary and a fallback. INDIVIDUAL is a person hiring for a
// personal need (wedding photographer, birthday DJ); ORGANIZATION is someone
// hiring on behalf of a company, brand, NGO, hotel, school or team. An
// INDIVIDUAL is never asked for an organization name, business size, PAN or
// registration — see the Business Verification backlog for progressive
// verification.
enum RepresentingType {
  ORGANIZATION
  INDIVIDUAL
}

// Answers "What is this for?" on business onboarding, right after picking
// which provider categories they're looking for — drives whether the
// Industry step (below) is shown at all: only BRAND_MARKETING and
// CONTENT_CREATION need an industry to match against, the rest (an event,
// wedding, one-off shoot, ...) don't.
enum BusinessPurpose {
  BRAND_MARKETING
  CONTENT_CREATION
  EVENT
  WEDDING
  PHOTOSHOOT
  PERFORMANCE
  COLLABORATION
  OTHER
}

// What kind of organization is hiring — ORGANIZATION-only, asked right after
